**Proposition 9.1 (activation is indispensable to current identification).**
At an authorized old Ready, the source/variable-input/ordinal triple alone
does not identify the enlarged runtime after one further row. A memory
consisting only of already published historical packages also fails the
$Q_+$ kernel at the first activation boundary.

Proof. From that Ready take its ordinary continuation Advance or Install.
Reservation/entry work precedes the first old frame IN. Both alternatives
are non-IN occurrences with one receipt and no variable
input or source change. Their resulting triples therefore agree. Their
mode/PC and enabled subsequent work differ: one begins original ingress,
the other the fresh bootstrap. Thus a replay selector omitting the
activation choice is insufficient. Before and immediately after Install
there is still no published historical package, while Install is enabled
only before. Hence the package-directory-only view merges task-distinct
cuts. The actual phase frontier and unchanged complete old frames in
Lemma 5.3 distinguish these cuts without a premature manifest. This
does not refute RCA's eventual acquired-service theorem. ∎

